<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banza Bakwai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banza Bakwai, the 'seven bastards', were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> and neighbouring kingdoms that Hausa tradition regarded as less legitimate than the seven true Hausa states descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayajidda">Bayajidda</a>. They usually include Zamfara, Kebbi, Yauri, Gwari, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a>, Kwararafa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a>. Several, such as Kebbi and Zamfara, were powerful states in their own right.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banza-bakwai.jpg" alt="Banza Bakwai" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zykasaa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AFRhausalandas.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
